WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys, Action Bronson
has been on this show

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
a great many times,
and we love Action.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what we love
most about Action is,

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
you never know what's
going to happen when he's here

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:15.949
up to and including
you never know if he'll be here.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:20.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I am sorry to say that
tonight, he is not.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:24.891 line:92%
And he's welcome back anytime.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:29.062
But I will say, when you'r
supposed to be on a talk sho

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.264 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and then you don't show,

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:38.238 line:92%
[bleep] that's capricious.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we've got
a fall-back plan, you guys

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.113 line:92%
This is a big deal for us.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.115 line:92%
I can't believe we got him

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:53.520
You know him not just from doing
cue cards at our show.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.488 line:92%
He's also been doing cue cards

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:59.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
at "Saturday Night Live"
since 1990.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Please --

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.829
Well, just welcome from
backstage -- He was here.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:03.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's always here.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.199 line:92%
Please welcome Wally Feresten.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, my God.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey!

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey! Steve! Mike!

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
How you guys doing?
How you doing?

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
How's everybody doing?
I know everybody.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Take a seat.
You know everybody.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.683 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah. I kind of had
a rough entrance there.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I was going to say,
seven years in,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've never had
anybody crash into the door.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm used to coming
in from that way, not --

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, it's still just a door

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.163 line:92%
-Yeah. That's a good point

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
if you go through one door

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should be able to
get through most.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, actually,
I'm bummed out,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause when you came out,
I thought we

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
should have done that --
You know sometimes when people

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.908
hit their first home run,
none of the players clap?

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Applaud. Yeah.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.610 line:92%
-I should have told the crew

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't clap when
Wally comes out."

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.046 line:92%
-That would have been funny.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wally, thank you so much
for being here.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:58.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, a lot of people
think you just hold cue cards.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.954 line:92%
You actually have a compan

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.856
and you do cue cards for
a lot of different shows.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to ask real quick
you had to come up with

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
a name for company that
encompassed everything it did,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.933 size:84% position:42%
and it had to be a name
that would immediately

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.468 line:92%
make people think, "That guy

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously knows
what he's doing."

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you went throug
hundreds of names.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.339 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I remember you doing it.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you please tell everybod
what you came up with?

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New York City Cue Cards.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I finished on.
Probably wasn't 100 names.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was probably the first thin
that came to my mind.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"That's perfect."

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait. What about
Cue Cards by Wally?

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.786 line:92%
-Well, that's my other company

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, tell everybody about
Cue Cards by Wally.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cue Cards by Wally I starte
during the pandemic,

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.826 size:81% position:41% line:92%
when I wasn't working.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.728 size:84% position:42%
I was bored and I was
sitting around at home.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.864
And I thought, "If I can't d
cue cards for celebrities,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.732 line:92%
like yourself and other people

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.735
"why don't I do personalized
cue cards for people at home."

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because they can't
go to birthday parties

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.037 line:92%
and they couldn't go to parties.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of a
perfect time to do it.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And these are on the iconic
"SNL" cue cards.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Same cue cards
written all by me,

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I was shocked to think
people would want,

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:02.115 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but they did.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And every time I sent one ou
and I looked at it

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I sent it out,
I was like,

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They're really going to b
disappointed, I think,

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's just really marker
on a piece of cardboard."

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But every time they got it,
they were like,

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.394
"This is the greatest thin
I've ever gotten in my life.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.028 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And they loved it.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really nice when
someone is willing to admi

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
that their product is just
marker on a piece of cardboard

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It really is.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I think that's one
of the things we love about yo

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:25.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is your honesty.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:31.344
The other thing I want to sa
is, you know, this is no jok

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Cue Cards by Wally
is a big deal.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.115 size:84% position:42%
I, in my dressing room,
have my last "SNL" --

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:39.953
I have the cue card from my good
night at "Weekend Update."

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:44.090
And, sort of famously, a lot o
cast members want a cue card

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a lot hosts
take them home with them.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'll put together
a package, usually, for hosts,

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.396
and sometimes, I'll say, "Hey,
do you want some souvenirs?"

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.264 line:92%
So, I just sent -- It's funny.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sent Carey Mulligan
a package of her cue cards

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I did
the Elon Musk show.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got home,
and there was a note --

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
a handwritten letter
from Ireland.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:02.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it was
from somebody else.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it was after the show,
and I was really tired

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.379 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and I was reading it.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I still thought it was
from somebody else,

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:09.515 line:92%
and it was from Carey Mulligan

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
thanking me for
sending her the cards,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she was like,
"I felt like it was a dream,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.522
but having these kind of make it
feel like it was reality."

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:17.257 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So it was really nice.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who was the
Irish person you thought

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.961 line:92%
you were getting a letter from

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
Halfway through a letter
from Carey Mulligan,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and you're like --

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:28.835
-There was an Irish guy that
connected with me on Faceboo

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
that said he was
coming to see this show,

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:33.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was the week after
we shut down for the pandemic.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-So he couldn't come over.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I sent him an Irish --
You made a joke about

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
Irish people and drinking,
like you normally do.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And I sent him those cards.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought this was
a thank-you note for that.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's very nice.
Well, there you go.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's why I was confused
but then --

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.355 line:92%
-I don't -- That wasn't a joke

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was based on
something in the news.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, okay. Okay.
-Yeah.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
I'm not just going at them

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:56.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
These aren't just, like,
ad hominem attacks

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.197 line:92%
on our friends across the seas

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, so, this is --
I want to talk

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.302 line:92%
because I actually do think --

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, one of the questions
I get asked a lot --

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
We used to do a Q&amp;A
when we had an audience here

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a thing that people
are genuinely fascinated by is

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:13.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
why does our show use cue card
instead of teleprompter?

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:13.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, the cue-card shows, as I
understand it, are --

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
They all kind of come from
the "SNL" tree.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Correct.
-Jimmy uses cue cards.

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
Conan used cue cards.
-Yep.

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did him.
We use cue cards.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think it is,
that's how we came up.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.028 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When hosts come on "SNL,"
a lot of times,

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's the first time
they have used cue cards.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.102 line:92%
-So what is the first thing --

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:36.936 line:92%
And I've watched this happen

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
But explain to people
the first thing you have to do

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.006
when a host gets there,
insofar as the cue cards.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, first of all, I ask the
how their eyesight is,

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause that's
the most important thing -

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:44.844 size:88% position:44% line:92%
if they can see alright.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I'll show them
a normal-sized printing card

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.382
and then I'll show them a little
bigger-sized printing card

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
just so we can
get off on the right --

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then I ask if
they've ever worked with

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:53.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
cue cards before.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.587 line:92%
And most of them haven't.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's just a basic talkin
about, you know,

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:58.524 size:75% position:38% line:92%
seeing them alright.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.060 size:88% position:44%
And then, you know, Don,
the director of "SNL" --

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
between me and him,
and then we'll talk to the

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:04.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
about more specific things
about how to play them

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
where to look at them

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
and don't memorize anything,
that kind of thing

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And if you had --
And, sometimes,

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:12.038
you have a host who thinks
they're not going to need cards,

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, over the course of
the week, they --

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.574 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah. Like, you know,
Matthew McConaughey.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was the nicest guy,
but he was like,

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Eh, I'm not going to use
the cue cards."

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:18.878 line:92%
And I was like, "No problem.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll be over here,
you know, if you need me."

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:24.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then by like
Friday afternoon, he was like,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:27.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
"So, where are you going to be
in case I need them?"

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I was --
"I'll be over there."

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.590
And he was like, "Okay,
just in case I need you."

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, on Saturday,
he was like,

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Alright, where are you
going to be for each sketch?

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he thanked me after
and he apologized.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "You don't need to
apologize."

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:39.899
But he was like, "I didn't
understand how inclusive

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
the cards were
and how much it changed."

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.301 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's the thing.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
The real reason you can't
memorize on the show

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:45.505 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is that there's no --

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It changes so much.
-You just changes so much.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:47.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:52.879 size:81% position:41%
-You had a moment that
I always recall fondly

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:53.980 size:78% position:39% line:92%
with Charles Barkley.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a
Saturday rehearsal, yeah?

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:56.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Correct.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you want to
tell everybody what went down?

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so, Chris Kelly,
the stage manager,

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:01.687 line:92%
came over to me and said,

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Charles wants to play
a practical joke on the cast

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:06.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's going to
pretend to be mad at you.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one knows about this
but me and you."

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:09.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like,
"Are you good with that?"

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Yeah, sure.
Why not?" You know?

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we went out there
for a sketch,

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
and right in
the middle of the sketch,

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
Charles breaks character
and he starts yelling at me.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:20.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Wally, I can't -
Hold the cards still.

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can't see them."

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.876 line:92%
HE's like -- And he stormed off.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:26.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people were like --
-I fully bought it.

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.680 line:92%
-People were, like, shocked.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will Forte actually yelled
"Hit him" to Charles.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.119 line:92%
He told Charles to hit me.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:36.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- Which I took
umbrage to a little bit.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:37.723 line:92%
-Yeah, I mean, of course.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
That meant that
he thought it was true,

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:40.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he finally thought you
were getting --

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.362
-Yeah, he was like,
"Wally is gonna finally get hit,

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:44.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
get what's coming to him."

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Charles stopped
halfway off the stage

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then said,
"I'm just busting."

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everybody laughed,
and it was great.

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:51.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was beet-red,
even though I knew about it.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't -- You know,
everyone was staring at me

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:53.840 line:92%
And then I went over to Will

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"What the hell, Will?"

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like,
"Oh, I was just trying to

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.646 size:84% position:42% line:92%
diffuse the situation."

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.681 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:04.517
-I remember it was like,
"What the [bleep] Wally?!"

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:05.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was very --
-Yeah.

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:06.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think the part
that I can't believe

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
all these years later is,
I'm like,

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:12.158
"I can't believe Charles Barkley
was such a good actor."

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:08:12.592 --> 00:08:14.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, by the way,
I didn't yell "Hit him,"

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.731
but, at the same time, like,
if he had started hitting you,

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.333 line:92%
I would not have done anything

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
mostly -- Not because
I don't love you.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a big guy.
-Yeah, he's a big guy.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:24.770 line:92%
I get it. No, I understand

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.174 size:78% position:39%
-And you do sometimes
move the cue cards.

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:31.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know it and I know it.
You move the cue cards.

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:33.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wally, you know,
and one of the other reasons -

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I want to be sincere
for a second --

00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:39.652
that we don't use a teleprompter
is, we have a deep friendship.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been holding cards,
and I always say,

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
like 95% of the words that I
have said on television

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:48.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
over a career that's
almost like 20 years long no

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
are cards that
you've been holding up.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:54.467 size:88% position:44%
And I remember that when
I did the Golden Globes,

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:58.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had you there just in case,
standing in a tuxedo

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.172 line:92%
next to the teleprompter,

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:01.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
just in case
something went wrong.

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:02.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I never returned that
tuxedo, by the way.

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:05.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You never returned it?
-No, I kept it.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:06.712 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's okay, right?

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:09.715 line:92%
-Well, it's very unfair for yo

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:13.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say it now,
in front of America.

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:14.253 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is Wally.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:19.025 line:92%
You can see him most nights --

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:20.960 line:92%
most nights on "Late Night."

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:27.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
Action, again, we do hope
you come back soon, as well.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

